Return 3-tuples from _get_per_token_logps_and_entropies for TRL >= 1.8.

TRL 1.8 extended _get_per_token_logps_and_entropies to return
(logps, entropies, aux_loss) — aux_loss is the MoE router load-balancing
loss. All call sites in TRL's GRPOTrainer (and hence in the generated
unsloth_compiled_cache/UnslothGRPOTrainer.py) unpack three values:

    old_per_token_logps, _, _ = self._get_per_token_logps_and_entropies(...)

Unsloth's replacement still returned 2-tuples, crashing the first
training step with:

    ValueError: not enough values to unpack (expected 3, got 2)

Return aux_loss=None (unsloth's efficient path never computes it; TRL
only consumes it when the model config enables router aux loss).

Patching the template here (instead of the generated cache file) survives
cache regeneration.
--- a/unsloth/models/rl_replacements.py	2026-07-06 19:43:33.523301146 +0200
+++ b/unsloth/models/rl_replacements.py	2026-07-06 19:43:33.542408211 +0200
@@ -1192,7 +1192,7 @@
         # if True: # os.environ.get('UNSLOTH_USE_NEW_MODEL', '0') == '0':
         #     return None, None  # logps, entropies Unsloth efficient GRPO
         if compute_efficient:
-            return None, None
+            return None, None, None
         else:
             if not hasattr(self, "_autocast_dtype"):
                 self._autocast_dtype = (
@@ -1918,7 +1918,7 @@
 
             os.environ["UNSLOTH_RETURN_HIDDEN_STATES"] = "0"
 
-            return logprobs.detach(), entropies  # logps, entropies
+            return logprobs.detach(), entropies, None  # logps, entropies, aux_loss
             # input_ids = input_ids[:, -logits_to_keep:]
             # For transformers<=4.48, logits_to_keep argument isn't supported, so here we drop logits ourselves.
             # See https://github.com/huggingface/trl/issues/2770
